{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01VifXBphMEJUFmgwJ5Gs8T3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\n2\t# B-Tree Library\n3\t\n4\t## Introduction\n5\tThis library offers a versatile B-Tree implementation in C, ideal for efficient key-value storage and retrieval. It supports various key types, making it suitable for a wide range of applications.\n6\t\n7\t## Building the Library\n8\tCompile the library with the following command:\n9\t\n10\t```bash\n11\tmake\n12\t```\n13\t\n14\t## Usage Examples\n15\t\n16\t### Adding and Finding an Entry\n17\tThis example demonstrates how to add an entry to the B-Tree and retrieve it.\n18\t\n19\t```c\n20\tbtree_t* btree = new_btree();\n21\tadd_entry(btree, \"entry_1\", sizeof(\"entry_1\"), \"value_1\", sizeof(\"value_1\"));\n22\tvalue_t* value = find_entry(btree, \"entry_1\", sizeof(\"entry_1\"));\n23\t// Use 'value' as needed\n24\tfree_tree(&btree);\n25\t```\n26\t\n27\t### Working with Multiple Entries\n28\tHere's how to add multiple entries and list them.\n29\t\n30\t```c\n31\tbtree_t* btree = new_btree();\n32\tadd_entry(btree, \"entry_1\", sizeof(\"entry_1\"), \"value_1\", sizeof(\"value_1\"));\n33\t// ... Add more entries\n34\tentry_list_t* list = list_entries(btree);\n35\t// Iterate over 'list' to access entries\n36\tfree_entry_list(&list);\n37\tfree_tree(&btree);\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\t### Removing an Entry\n41\tThis example shows how to remove an entry from the B-Tree.\n42\t\n43\t```c\n44\tbtree_t* btree = new_btree();\n45\tadd_entry(btree, \"entry_1\", sizeof(\"entry_1\"), \"value_1\", sizeof(\"value_1\"));\n46\tremove_entry(btree, \"entry_1\", sizeof(\"entry_1\"));\n47\t// 'entry_1' is now removed from the B-Tree\n48\tfree_tree(&btree);\n49\t```\n50\t\n51\t### Using Custom Key Types\n52\tThe B-Tree can handle various key types. Here's an example using an integer key.\n53\t\n54\t```c\n55\tbtree_t* btree = new_btree();\n56\tuint32_t int_key = 123;\n57\tadd_entry(btree, &int_key, sizeof(int_key), \"value_123\", sizeof(\"value_123\"));\n58\tvalue_t* value = find_entry(btree, &int_key, sizeof(int_key));\n59\t// Use 'value' as needed\n60\tfree_tree(&btree);\n61\t```\n62\t\n63\t### Adding Custom Structs\n64\tYou can also use custom structs as keys or values.\n65\t\n66\t```c\n67\ttypedef struct custom_key {\n68\t    uint32_t key_part1;\n69\t    uint32_t key_part2;\n70\t} custom_key_t;\n71\t\n72\tbtree_t* btree = new_btree();\n73\tcustom_key_t my_key = {1, 2};\n74\tadd_entry(btree, &my_key, sizeof(my_key), \"custom_value\", sizeof(\"custom_value\"));\n75\tvalue_t* value = find_entry(btree, &my_key, sizeof(my_key));\n76\t// Use 'value' as needed\n77\tfree_tree(&btree);\n78\t```\n79\t\n80\t## Contributions\n81\tContributions to improve this library are welcome. Feel free to submit pull requests or raise issues."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a1e97dc-8549-4a7b-886b-db8748f35852","uuid":"73f8b221-4e1b-42c1-adca-cb353814dd3c","timestamp":"2026-05-29T09:12:48.157Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/harvest-crust-5aiusC/project/c_src/README.md","content":"\n# B-Tree Library\n\n## Introduction\nThis library offers a versatile B-Tree implementation in C, ideal for efficient key-value storage and retrieval. It supports various key types, making it suitable for a wide range of applications.\n\n## Building the Library\nCompile the library with the following command:\n\n```bash\nmake\n```\n\n## Usage Examples\n\n### Adding and Finding an Entry\nThis example demonstrates how to add an entry to the B-Tree and retrieve it.\n\n```c\nbtree_t* btree = new_btree();\nadd_entry(btree, \"entry_1\", sizeof(\"entry_1\"), \"value_1\", sizeof(\"value_1\"));\nvalue_t* value = find_entry(btree, \"entry_1\", sizeof(\"entry_1\"));\n// Use 'value' as needed\nfree_tree(&btree);\n```\n\n### Working with Multiple Entries\nHere's how to add multiple entries and list them.\n\n```c\nbtree_t* btree = new_btree();\nadd_entry(btree, \"entry_1\", sizeof(\"entry_1\"), \"value_1\", sizeof(\"value_1\"));\n// ... Add more entries\nentry_list_t* list = list_entries(btree);\n// Iterate over 'list' to access entries\nfree_entry_list(&list);\nfree_tree(&btree);\n```\n\n### Removing an Entry\nThis example shows how to remove an entry from the B-Tree.\n\n```c\nbtree_t* btree = new_btree();\nadd_entry(btree, \"entry_1\", sizeof(\"entry_1\"), \"value_1\", sizeof(\"value_1\"));\nremove_entry(btree, \"entry_1\", sizeof(\"entry_1\"));\n// 'entry_1' is now removed from the B-Tree\nfree_tree(&btree);\n```\n\n### Using Custom Key Types\nThe B-Tree can handle various key types. Here's an example using an integer key.\n\n```c\nbtree_t* btree = new_btree();\nuint32_t int_key = 123;\nadd_entry(btree, &int_key, sizeof(int_key), \"value_123\", sizeof(\"value_123\"));\nvalue_t* value = find_entry(btree, &int_key, sizeof(int_key));\n// Use 'value' as needed\nfree_tree(&btree);\n```\n\n### Adding Custom Structs\nYou can also use custom structs as keys or values.\n\n```c\ntypedef struct custom_key {\n    uint32_t key_part1;\n    uint32_t key_part2;\n} custom_key_t;\n\nbtree_t* btree = new_btree();\ncustom_key_t my_key = {1, 2};\nadd_entry(btree, &my_key, sizeof(my_key), \"custom_value\", sizeof(\"custom_value\"));\nvalue_t* value = find_entry(btree, &my_key, sizeof(my_key));\n// Use 'value' as needed\nfree_tree(&btree);\n```\n\n## Contributions\nContributions to improve this library are welcome. Feel free to submit pull requests or raise issues.","numLines":81,"startLine":1,"totalLines":81}}}
